<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reşid Mehmed Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reşid Mehmed Pasha was an Ottoman general and grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-ii">Mahmud II</a>. He restored central authority in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/missolonghi">Missolonghi</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a> and defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-pasha-bushati">Mustafa Pasha Bushati</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Shkodër</a> in 1831. In 1836 he led the campaign that forced Mir Muhammad of the Soran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> to surrender. He was defeated by Egyptian forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a> in 1832.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/resid-mehmed-pasha.jpg" alt="Reşid Mehmed Pasha" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Boggi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_del_pasci%C3%A0_Rescild_-_Giovanni_Boggi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
